# 07 — Modern Coding Patterns

Use the most reasonable, up-to-date coding patterns for the language version the project uses.

In TypeScript, examples include `map` and `filter` instead of index loops, `async`/`await` instead of promise chains, and optional chaining (`?.`). In Java, an example is stream APIs instead of for-loops.
